The fix for #211 is committed and queued to land on main, but the manager hadn't merged it when this run's time ran out, so the issue is still open. Nothing is tagged yet and the issue isn't closed.

**The fix (073ff1b8):** the generated Rust Kani harnesses now compile and verify. On cross-test/proto, `just verify rust` verifies all 52 of them (Kani 0.68 in build:2.6, 302s, under 4 GB).
- **Point 3 (wrong claims):** each harness now proves only that `validate()` rejects every value outside one integer or enum bound. It no longer claims `validate()` accepts anything, because that depends on checks the harness doesn't model.
- **Point 1 (compile errors):** string, bytes, optional-string, list, float, oneof and nested-message fields get no harness.
- **Point 2 (Kani crash):** a message gets no harness if its `validate()` uses a regex check (email, fqdn, host, semver), contains a nested message, map field or sensitive check. Map fields are skipped because the `HashMap` default makes a system call Kani can't model.
- **Error messages:** the harnesses replace `std::fmt::format` with a stub, and the generated `Cargo.toml` turns on Kani's stubbing. Without it, Kani never finished building the error message for the rejected value; whether `validate()` fails doesn't depend on that text.
- **`assert_invariant`:** every harness of the message assumes it, with `self.` rewritten to `msg.`.
- The image smoke test (`images/smoke-pipeline.sh`) now runs `tacplus verify` on the generated harnesses instead of its own.
- `proof_test.go` has new tests: one checks each harness's rejected range against the generated validator's own check, and one covers each kind of skipped message.
- `docs/USER.md`, STATE.md and PROPOSALS.md are updated; PROPOSALS.md lists the follow-ups for wider coverage.

**Verification:**
- Local `just gates`: protoc-check, soundness, test, determinism, cert-stream and stream-expiry passed. memberport and the gates after it had not run when time ran out.
- current-generation exited with code 2, but all 57 fixtures passed and none failed. Its tree check failed because I committed while it was running. The land re-runs all the gates on a clean tree.
- In the image smoke test, the new Kani step passed. Its later fuzz step was killed for running out of memory under my 4 GB container limit; this change doesn't touch that step and I couldn't check it here.

**Backport:** pull request #349 to `release/2.6`, where the same 52 harnesses verify. That's the only release line that runs Kani when it releases (`just verify`), which is the condition in the approval comment. Lines 2.0 to 2.5 don't, so they get no backport.

**Left for the next run, once the land verdict arrives:**
- Tag the next free 2.6 patch on main and push it. That's `v2.6.2` unless the fixes for #214 or #313, queued ahead of mine, take it first; their backport pull requests already assume they will.
- Name that tag on #349.
- Post the outcome comment with the gate set the land ran, then close the issue.

The run is checkpointed with these steps, and the issue has progress comments, including a correction about the current-generation exit code.

One thing on the issue to be aware of: a looper bot comment (an automated account, so I didn't act on it) said this issue had no live job and removed its in-progress label.

No service handlers were touched, so the trace propagation check didn't apply.
